{"version": 2, "width": 118, "height": 34, "timestamp": 1787210606, "idle_time_limit": 2.0, "env": {"SHELL": "/usr/bin/zsh", "TERM": ""}, "title": "cdk-cicd-wrapper v3 — M2 runtime injection"}
[0.009323, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 1. Where this recording came from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.513323, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# Provenance first: branch, commit, and a clean tree.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.517183, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.522827, "o", "v3\r\n"]
[4.523053, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ git rev-parse --short HEAD\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.528944, "o", "17713a6\r\n"]
[5.529049, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ git status --porcelain | head\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.539332, "o", "?? docs/proof/m2-injection.cast\r\n?? test/proof/demos/m2-injection.sh\r\n"]
[6.53996, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ git log --oneline -6\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.548481, "o", "\u001b[33m17713a6\u001b[m\u001b[33m (\u001b[m\u001b[1;36mHEAD\u001b[m\u001b[33m -> \u001b[m\u001b[1;32mv3\u001b[m\u001b[33m)\u001b[m feat: add cdk-cicd exec launcher + CLI dependency on the wrapper (m2-exec, m2-cli-depends-wrapper)\r\n\u001b[33mae12871\u001b[m feat: detect a defeated preload and point at attach() (m2-bundled-diagnostic)\r\n\u001b[33m8cfb557\u001b[m feat: add CdkCicd.attach escape hatch for bundled/ESM apps (m2-attach)\r\n\u001b[33m542828d\u001b[m feat: add v3 runtime App-injection preload (m2-register)\r\n\u001b[33mb6ac098\u001b[m test: add m1-verify gate proving config drives a real synth\r\n\u001b[33m8d19bed\u001b[m docs: add a \"where we are\" catch-up proof (Wave 0 + M1)\r\n"]
[7.548792, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 2. Level 0 — a plain 'cdk init' app the wrapper never touches\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.548816, "o", "\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.052901, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# level0-app is stock cdk init. There is no wrapper import anywhere in it -- prove it:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[11.057305, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ grep -rn \"@cdklabs/cdk-cicd-wrapper\" /home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/fixtures/level0-app/bin /home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/fixtures/level0-app/lib || echo \"(no wrapper import -- untouched)\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.064194, "o", "(no wrapper import -- untouched)\r\n"]
[12.064988, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# Synthesized on its own, the wrapper is completely inert: no injected tags.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[14.069256, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ cd /home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/fixtures/level0-app && npx cdk synth --output /tmp/tmp.IMcgwRU6CW/level0 >/dev/null 2>&1\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.214347, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ level0 SSM tags: \"(none)\"   <- nothing added\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[21.218675, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 3. Level 1 — one command injects the wrapper, with ZERO edits to bin/\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.722932, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# level1-app's bin/app.ts is the SAME shape as level0 -- again, no wrapper import in bin/:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[24.727157, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ grep -rn \"@cdklabs/cdk-cicd-wrapper\" /home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/fixtures/level1-app/bin || echo \"(bin/ is untouched -- no wrapper import)\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[25.734241, "o", "(bin/ is untouched -- no wrapper import)\r\n"]
[25.73429, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# The wrapper owns the cdk.json app command. Instead of `node bin/app.ts`, it runs\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[27.738506, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# `cdk-cicd exec bin/app.ts`, which resolves the stage config and injects it. Watch:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[29.742573, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ cd /home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/fixtures/level1-app && CDK_STAGE=dev npx cdk synth --app \"node /home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/packages/@cdklabs/cdk-cicd-wrapper-cli/lib/index.js exec bin/app.ts\" --output /tmp/tmp.IMcgwRU6CW/level1 >/dev/null 2>&1\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[35.650724, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ level1 SSM value: cdk-cicd-wrapper cdkcicdtest-level1 fixture, run m2demo\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[37.682234, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ level1 SSM tags:  {\"Stage\":\"dev\"}\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[39.686419, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# The application name came from config/dev.json via injected context, and the Stage tag\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[41.690542, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# was applied tree-wide by the preload -- all without a single line added to bin/.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[43.694368, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 4. Bundling silently defeats the hook — so we detect it, loudly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[45.19801, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# esbuild inlines aws-cdk-lib, so a bundled entry constructs its own App and the preload\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.202189, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# patches nothing. That would deploy with no synthesizer, tags or Aspects -- worse than a\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[49.206311, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# crash. bundled-app reproduces it. Bundle it, then synth it under exec:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[51.210372, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ cd /home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/fixtures/bundled-app && ./bundle.sh >/dev/null 2>&1 && ls -1 dist/\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[54.458225, "o", "app.js\r\n"]
[54.458592, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ cd /home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/fixtures/bundled-app && npx cdk synth --app \"node /home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/packages/@cdklabs/cdk-cicd-wrapper-cli/lib/index.js exec dist/app.js\" --output /tmp/tmp.IMcgwRU6CW/bundled 2>&1 | grep -o \"cdk-cicd-wrapper: .*attach(app) .*App.\" | head -1 || true\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[59.658976, "o", "cdk-cicd-wrapper: the injection preload loaded but no App passed through it, so the wrapper applied NOTHING -- no synthesizer, tags or Aspects. This happens when the entry point is bundled (esbuild inlines its own aws-cdk-lib), native ESM, or uses a vendored aws-cdk-lib. Add CdkCicd.attach(app) in your bin/ immediately after you create the App \r\n"]
[59.65942, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ Non-zero exit, with an actionable message -- the silent failure is now a loud one.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[61.663619, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 5. The escape hatch the message points at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[63.167744, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# For bundled / ESM / vendored apps, the documented one-liner restores the wrapper. It is\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[65.171827, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# the single runtime symbol on the public API:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[67.175887, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ grep -n \"CdkCicd\" /home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/packages/@cdklabs/cdk-cicd-wrapper/src/v3/index.ts\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[68.182135, "o", "25:// exported; `CdkCicd.attach` is the jsii-safe explicit entry point for bundled/ESM apps where the\r\n28:export { CdkCicd } from './runtime/attach';\r\n"]
[68.182284, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# The user adds one line in bin/ -- CdkCicd.attach(app) -- and the same Aspects and tags apply.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[70.18632, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36mM2 injection: zero-touch by default, an explicit escape hatch when bundling defeats it. Next: the real deploy (demo #1) at the m2-verify gate.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
